From: Hoki local development <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: coalesce non-rewindable DSP copy writes

Prevent short native-protocol chunks from monopolizing DSP packet slots.
Only enable when the configured safeguard disables hardware rewinds.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Hoki DSP copy driver workaround]

--- a/src/modules/alsa/alsa-sink.c
+++ b/src/modules/alsa/alsa-sink.c
@@ -894,8 +894,15 @@
 
 /*         pa_log_debug("%lu frames to write", (unsigned long) frames); */
 
-            if (u->memchunk.length <= 0)
-                pa_sink_render(u->sink, n_bytes, &u->memchunk);
+            if (u->memchunk.length <= 0) {
+                /* Non-rewindable DSP copy devices have bounded packet slots.
+                 * Coalesce short client chunks to avoid blocking before the
+                 * logical hardware ring is full. */
+                if (u->rewind_safeguard >= u->hwbuf_size)
+                    pa_sink_render_full(u->sink, n_bytes, &u->memchunk);
+                else
+                    pa_sink_render(u->sink, n_bytes, &u->memchunk);
+            }
 
             pa_assert(u->memchunk.length > 0);
 
